  "title": "Unique Characteristics of Surah al-Ikhlas & Some Other Short Surahs",
  "data": "Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said, “If you recite [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) seventy times over a dead person, it would not be surprising if life were breathed into him again.”\nImam Musa al-Kazim (a.s.) is reported to have said, “A tremendous reward will be recorded for a boy who recites [Surah al-Falaq](A117) and [Surah al-Nas](A118) three times each, and [Surah al-Tawhid](A116) one hundred times, every night. If this is not possible, reciting Surah al-Tawhid fifty times instead of one hundred is acceptable. A boy who keeps this up regularly (or on whose behalf someone keeps reciting them) will be under divine protection until his death.”\nShaykh al-Kulayni has reported that Imam Ja'far al-Sadiq (a.s.) said to al-Mufaddal: Guard yourself from all people with “Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim” and Surah al-Tawhid, reciting it in front of you, behind you, to your right, to your left, above you and beneath you. If you are summoned before a tyrannical ruler, recite it three times the moment you look at him, and hold your left hand closed. Keep this up until you leave him.\nExplanation: holding the left hand closed may mean keeping its fingers pressed together; or the expression may mean, as some scholars understand it, to keep reciting the Surah over and over until one leaves."
}
